# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Test / lint / type caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# ── Agent runtime state (per-project, never committed) ────────────────────────
# Sessions, audit log, checkpoints, snapshots and per-project skills live here.
.agentic/

# ── Project-local working files (not part of the public repo) ─────────────────
backups/

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here needs an API key — the project is Ollama-only by design — but a
# stray credential file is the one mistake a public repo cannot take back, so the
# net is cast wider than this project strictly needs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json

# ── Agent config, if it ever lands inside the repo ─────────────────────────────
# These normally live in $HOME (see the note at the bottom). This rule only matters
# if HOME is redirected here — which is exactly what a test harness does.
.agentic_1a_*

# ── Editor / tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.serena/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Merge / patch artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.orig
*.rej

# ── OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Note ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent also writes to your HOME directory, outside this repo:
#   ~/.agentic_1a_history            input history (all projects)
#   ~/.agentic_1a_params.json        /parameters settings
#   ~/.agentic_1a_mcp.json           MCP server configuration
#   ~/.agentic_1a_default_model.txt  persisted default model
#   ~/.agentic_1a_models.json        model roles (failover, architect, vision)
#   ~/.agentic_1a_skills/            your global skills
#   ~/.agentic_imessage.json         iMessage bridge configuration
# Nothing there is ever committed. See the Privacy section of the manual.

# ── Model ranking campaign ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scores.json is kept: it is the evidence behind every number in RESULTS.md, and it
# holds only structured metadata (21 KB, no page text).
# The raw run directories are excluded for a reason beyond size: they contain the full
# text of third-party news articles and vendor blog posts fetched during the search and
# report tasks. Republishing someone else's article body in a public repo is not ours
# to do, and it would be the bulk of the ~3 MB.
benchmarks/model_ranking/results/*
!benchmarks/model_ranking/results/scores.json

# The A/B tree is excluded for exactly the same reason, and it was NOT covered by the rule
# above: that one names `results/` only, so ~100 run directories of third-party article text
# sat untracked-but-committable for a day. Same content, same reason, its own line.
benchmarks/model_ranking/results_ab/
benchmarks/model_ranking/ab_run*.log

# generated by CI when filtering optional deps
requirements-ci.txt
